# Superseded DECIPHER-based reference-audit approach (2026-08-07) -- kept locally
# for reference during the BLAST-based redesign, deliberately not committed.
# See ecosystem_docs/REENTRY_PROMPT_blast_based_reference_quality.md.
archive_decipher_reference_audit/

# Orphaned unified-likelihood-pipeline entry point (2026-09-09) -- compute_
# likelihoods()/model_likelihoods() had zero real callers anywhere; moved
# intact for reference, deliberately not committed. See TaxaLikely/CLAUDE.md's
# top session note.
archive_unused_likelihood_entrypoint/

# build_site_reference() (2026-09-09) -- a high-level fetch -> audit -> export
# wrapper found to have zero real callers anywhere in the monorepo (every real
# production workflow builds its reference database by calling
# fetch_ncbi_reference_sequences()/audit_barcode_coverage() directly). Kept
# locally as a record of the design, deliberately not committed, matching the
# DECIPHER precedent above. write_reference_fasta() -- its one internal
# caller -- was investigated in the same pass and kept LIVE/exported: it's a
# generic, standalone, round-trippable (with read_reference_fasta()) FASTA
# export utility with its own dedicated test coverage, not tightly coupled to
# build_site_reference()'s own output shape, and is this package's only
# reference-export capability -- archiving it too would have been a real
# capability loss, not just dead-code cleanup. See TaxaLikely/CLAUDE.md's
# 2026-09-09 session note and ecosystem_docs/NAME_CHANGE_HISTORY.md.
archive_unused_reference_wrappers/

# Coverage-filter calibration pair (2026-09-09) -- calibrate_coverage_filter()/
# coverage_threshold() archived (not deleted): a real A/B test on full-scale
# PtConception 12S data found a real H1 win-rate improvement (54.9%->65.1%,
# reproduced 55.1%->65.8%) on queries the filter is willing to answer, but a
# real, quantified cost (134/691 species, 19.4%, lose every training pair at
# the calibrated threshold; 25.1% of real evaluation queries end up
# unresolved) -- the same hard-exclusion-on-an-imperfect-proxy pattern this
# ecosystem has already relearned twice (apply_coverage_constraints()'s
# zero->relabel fix, filter_gbif_quality()'s exclude_institution->
# flag_institution fix). The one separable value (a Youden's-J diagnostic on
# whether coverage predicts pair quality) is a standard statistic that
# doesn't need a dedicated exported function. Kept locally for reference,
# deliberately not committed, matching the DECIPHER/likelihood-entrypoint/
# reference-wrapper precedents above. See TaxaLikely/CLAUDE.md's top session
# note and ecosystem_docs/NAME_CHANGE_HISTORY.md.
archive_unused_coverage_calibration/
